S={
"ai25_interspeech":("people-and-health","speaker-characteristics","age-and-development","A speaker system should recognize that a person's voice changes with age rather than treating time-varying identity as noise.","Longitudinal recordings mix biological change, channel variation, language, and recording history.","Train one speaker model on pooled recordings and assume a speaker embedding remains stationary.","Build a longitudinal English/Mandarin resource and measure how aging changes verification evidence.","Link recordings across years, then test verification as time gap, age group, and gender change.","EER and embedding cosine similarity turn identity preservation into separability and distance between same-speaker observations.","VoxAging contains 293 speakers with spans up to about 17 years; verification is evaluated with EER and cosine similarity, comparing ECAPA and ERes2Net systems.","The paper reports declining verification accuracy and embedding similarity as recordings move farther apart in time, with age and gender affecting the rate of change.","Speaker coverage, language balance, recording channels, gated data, and longitudinal confounding limit causal claims about biological aging."),
"jeong25_interspeech":("people-and-health","clinical-and-assistive-speech","clinical-speech-marker","A clinical audio classifier should distinguish medically meaningful lung-sound patterns without letting patient identity dominate.","Patient-specific acoustics and recording conditions can make a classifier memorize who was recorded instead of pathology.","Optimize ordinary cross-entropy on pooled recordings and trust aggregate accuracy.","Align patient-aware representations while separating normal and abnormal acoustic evidence.","Combine pretrained audio features with patient-aware alignment, cohesion-separation, and global-alignment losses before classification.","Similarity and separation losses reshape within-patient and across-class distances; sensitivity, specificity, and ICBHI score expose different errors.","The ICBHI 2017 corpus has 6,898 recordings and an official 60/40 split; five-run comparisons report sensitivity, specificity, and ICBHI score with backbone and loss ablations.","The paper reports improved ICBHI performance and more patient-balanced behavior with the proposed alignment losses.","Patient/device distribution, benchmark labels, acoustic conditions, and absent clinical deployment evaluation limit medical interpretation."),
"lemaguer25_interspeech":("evaluation-deployment-and-consequence","metrics-and-targets","auditability-and-contestability","A speech-synthesis listening claim should be inspectable and repeatable, not just summarized by one MOS number.","Subjective results depend on stimuli, participants, protocol, anchors, randomization, analysis, and reporting choices.","Report a mean listener score and assume reproducibility because the model and samples are named.","Decompose evaluation into a structured report and a recipe containing materials and decisions needed to repeat it.","Audit the goal, dataset and bias, participant cohort, protocol, analysis, conclusions, and limitations, then package evaluation assets and procedures.","The central object is an auditable mapping from hypothesis to stimuli, ratings, uncertainty, and conclusion.","This protocol paper contributes a checklist, evaluation-report structure, and reproducibility recipe rather than a new held-out model benchmark.","The paper reports a structured template intended to make subjective speech-synthesis studies more reproducible and limitations more visible.","A checklist cannot guarantee participant representativeness, perceptual validity, or exact replication when access differs."),
"liang25b_interspeech":("voice-generation-and-control","text-to-speech-and-content","intelligibility-naturalness","Video-to-audio generation must produce sound that matches what happens in a video and when it happens.","A generated sound can be semantically plausible but mistimed, or aligned but acoustically unrelated.","Prompt a generic text-to-audio model with a caption and ignore fine-grained event timing.","Use MLLM-augmented prompting and semantic-temporal adaptation for event identity and onset structure.","Video semantics guide the prompt while probabilistic temporal conditioning aligns generated events with visual onsets.","CLIP score measures semantic alignment and onset accuracy measures temporal agreement; their separation exposes two failures.","FoleyMaster is evaluated on VGGSound Plus with CLIP Score and onset accuracy, baselines, ablations, and a 20-participant pairwise study.","The paper reports gains across semantic and temporal metrics and user preference, with prompt/time components supported by ablations.","Automatic proxies, dataset distribution, event taxonomy, and a small listener study limit claims about real-world Foley usefulness."),
"takeuchi25_interspeech":("meaning-and-interaction","grounding-and-action","referential-grounding","An audio caption should identify the sound event a listener treats as the referent, not merely match common caption words.","Caption metrics reward n-gram overlap while missing semantic adequacy, and discrete representations can discard event details.","Feed a generic continuous audio embedding to a caption decoder and optimize only caption likelihood.","Use a semantic-rich audio representation tokenizer with multi-layer codebooks.","CLAP-ART converts audio into discrete representations learned from semantic audio features; a caption model conditions on those tokens.","CIDEr, SPICE, and SPIDEr compare generated language with references, but each is only a proxy for grounded event meaning.","CLAP-ART is tested on AudioCaps and a second audio-caption benchmark with BLEU, METEOR, ROUGE-L, CIDEr, SPICE, and SPIDEr, including six-run averages and codebook ablations.","The paper reports improved caption scores and a favorable multi-layer codebook tradeoff.","Reference-caption variability, language bias, metric disagreement, and no independent human grounding study limit claims."),
"tao25_interspeech":("listening-and-separation","source-separation-and-spatial-listening","spatial-filtering","A microphone array should locate several sources even when reverberation hides the direct path.","Reflections create false direction evidence and make direct-path bins sparse or unstable.","Search the whole spatial grid with a conventional beamformer or treat every bin as equally reliable.","Detect direct-path relative harmonic coefficients and use reliable spatial evidence for 3D localization.","Estimate relative harmonic structure, identify valid direct-path bins, and aggregate their directional evidence.","Mean absolute angular error measures localization distance; valid-bin proportion measures whether usable spatial observations were found.","Simulated reverberant scenes vary source count and T60, with recorded conditions also tested; MAEE and valid-bin proportion compare four baselines.","The paper reports lower localization error in most tested reverberant scenarios and improved robustness.","Array geometry, source count, room conditions, harmonic assumptions, and angular-error averaging limit transfer."),
"tisdale25_interspeech":("people-and-health","human-centered-evaluation","accessibility-fit","A real-time eye-gaze health tool should be usable by people with different motor and cognitive profiles, not only accurate for an average user.","Gaze error, fatigue, engagement, task difficulty, and individual movement interact, so one accuracy score misses usability.","Train one gaze predictor and evaluate only aggregate spatial error.","Combine accessible web-based interaction with task-specific metric families, cohort analysis, classification, and usability feedback.","Extract distance, velocity, saccade, and task metrics, compare cohorts, and use selected features in an AdaBoost classifier.","Feature selection and cross-validation turn gaze traces into a cohort-level decision, while survey ratings expose usability beyond classifier accuracy.","Kruskal-Wallis selection, k-fold validation, accuracy/F1, and survey ratings connect gaze traces to cohort decisions.","The paper reports AdaBoost at 0.89 accuracy and 0.67 F1 against 0.77 baseline, plus a 39-participant usability survey with 82% high engagement.","Cohort composition, task design, leakage risk, self-report, and absent clinical validation limit health claims."),
"xu25j_interspeech":("meaning-and-interaction","grounding-and-action","referential-grounding","Visual-guide audio captioning should remain semantically faithful when audio and visual streams do not line up.","Audiovisual mismatch can make a model overtrust the wrong modality and describe the wrong event fluently.","Train on perfectly synchronized pairs and assume test alignment is identical.","Use systematic audiovisual shuffling and semantic/temporal adaptation to train and test under mismatch.","Vary shuffle probability while semantic and temporal modules preserve event meaning and timing.","Caption metrics combine n-gram and semantic measures; repeated timed inference exposes accuracy and deployment cost.","The paper evaluates eight caption metrics across shuffle probabilities, ablates semantic/temporal components, varies video length, and averages timed inference.","The paper reports stronger semantic resilience under mismatch, with both modules contributing.","Synthetic shuffle may not represent real errors; caption variability and proxy metrics limit human-grounding claims.")
}
